  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Local Youth for Good Governance, Peace-Building, and Holistic Sustainable Livelihoods in Central Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project empowers 3,000 young people&#x2014;including young women and youth with disabilities&#x2014;in four target areas to strengthen their voice, leadership, and participation in local governance, peacebuilding, and livelihoods over 12 months. It enhances youth-inclusive governance structures, builds leadership and civic agency for 1,600 youth, improves the employability and economic resilience of 750 youth through skills training and entrepreneurship support, and establishes 10 peer-support groups offering psychosocial assistance and civic learning. Overall, the project aims to improve youth wellbeing, social cohesion, and institutional accountability.</narrative>
  </description>
